title: '[pallet-revive] `System.terminate` reverts when the contract balance cannot be released'

doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    `System.terminate` now reverts when the contract's balance has a lock, a freeze, or a hold
    under a reason other than the storage deposit, for example after a vested transfer to the
    contract. The revert message is "terminate pre-compile cannot release the contract's balance:
    it has a lock, freeze or hold", and the calling contract can catch it.

    Before, the call returned success and the beneficiary received the transferable balance, but
    the destruction at the end of the call stack could not burn the existential deposit and was
    skipped without an error. The contract stayed alive and callable.

    A lock placed on the contract later in the same transaction, after `System.terminate`
    returned, still makes the termination be skipped without an error. The `SELFDESTRUCT` opcode
    is unchanged.

- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet_revive::Error` gains the variant `TerminateBalanceLocked` (index `0x45`). `Error` is
    an exhaustive public enum, so code that matches on it exhaustively needs a new arm. No storage
    migration or configuration change is needed.

    The terminate precompile now charges `WeightInfo::seal_terminate_logic` a second time to pay
    for the dry run of the balance release, so a `System.terminate` call costs more weight. No
    benchmark changed.

    The `Terminate` fixture gains a `tryTerminate` function, which adds a variant to the
    generated `Terminate::TerminateCalls` enum in `pallet-revive-fixtures`.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-uapi
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: major
